NAME
    osarch-set - select active OS/architecture command roots

SYNOPSIS
    osarch-set
    osarch-set <osarch>

DESCRIPTION
    osarch-set selects the platform-specific sys, ext and ai command roots.

    With no operands, it detects the operating system and architecture through
    the m OS/architecture facility and selects the resulting normalized osarch.

    With one <osarch> operand, it selects that exact supported normalized
    identity instead of detecting the host. The identity has the form:
        <platform>-<architecture>

    Current normalized platforms are linux, macos and windows. Current
    normalized architectures are x86_64 and arm64.

    Before changing selectors, osarch-set rejects any selector pathname occupied
    by a non-symlink object. It then ensures the corresponding directories exist:
        bin/sys-<osarch>
        bin/ext-<osarch>
        bin/ai-<osarch>

    It creates or updates these relative selector symlinks:
        bin/sys-osarch -> sys-<osarch>
        bin/ext-osarch -> ext-<osarch>
        bin/ai-osarch  -> ai-<osarch>

    Successful selection produces no output.

    osarch-update is the compatibility command for detected-host selection and
    is equivalent to invoking osarch-set without operands.

EXIT STATUS
    0   Platform directories and selectors were updated.
    Non-zero status indicates invalid arguments, unsupported detected platform
        data, a selector conflict or filesystem/update failure.
